/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  reactions -- ammoniaStaged01_yield.  STOICHIOMETRY ONLY: a conversionReactor
  needs no kinetics, because its extent is SPECIFIED rather than computed.

  N2 + 3 H2 -> 2 NH3

  dH_rxn is NOT declared here, and must not be.  Every one of N2, H2 and NH3
  carries a standardThermochemistry block, so the engine derives the
  authoritative dH_rxn(T) = SUM nu_i * h_i(T) from the elements/formation
  datum (CLAUDE.md, "Heat of reaction -- ONE enthalpy base").  A dH_rxn key
  here would be a SECOND source of truth for a number that is already
  derivable, and the engine treats it as an announced override rather than an
  input.  It belongs only where a species lacks formation data.

  THE LIMITING REACTANT IS NITROGEN, and that is a modelling choice worth
  stating.  The loop's makeup is stoichiometric (H2:N2 = 3.0), so at the
  MAKEUP neither is limiting; inside the loop the recycle sets the converter
  inlet ratio, and `conversion` in the operation block is then read as the
  fraction of the inlet NITROGEN that reacts.  Per-pass conversion in the
  ammonia literature is normally quoted on nitrogen, so this is the reading a
  reader expects -- but it IS a reading, and the engine refuses a
  limitingReactant whose stoichiometric coefficient is not negative rather
  than guessing one.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
ammoniaSynthesis
{
    limitingReactant  N2;
    stoichiometry
    (
        { component N2;   nu -1; }
        { component H2;   nu -3; }
        { component NH3;  nu  2; }
    );
}
